# Example: FPV radio in USB joystick mode (for example BetaFPV LiteRadio 3). Copy to "<name of the radio>.cfg" (see DetectedDevices.txt)
# The right stick is the RHC pitch and roll, the rudder is the RHC yaw. The channels are assumed to be in the order
# aileron, elevator, throttle, rudder, AUX1, AUX2 (axes X, Y, Z, RX, RY, RZ): adjust it to your radio.
# AUX1 (3-position switch) is the RMS trigger: up = capture, down = release. AUX2 (2-position switch) is RATE HOLD.
INPUT	SUBDEVID	REVERSE	DEADZONE	EXPO	CENTER
RHC_ROLL	Axis X	false	0.05	0.3	0
RHC_PITCH	Axis Y	true	0.05	0.3	0
RHC_YAW	Axis RX	false	0.05	0.3	0
RMS_CAPTURE	Axis RY	false			
RMS_RELEASE	Axis RY	true			
RMS_RATE_HOLD	Axis RZ	false			
